# You only need this file when DEPLOYING to the team's LIVE Firebase project —
# day-to-day development uses the local emulators and the placeholder values in
# `.env`, and everyday testing uses the separate staging project
# (`.env.staging.local`, see its `.example` file). Most of the time you can
# ignore this file entirely. See DEPLOY.md for the full walkthrough.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.production.local` (git-ignored — never commit real
# keys) and fill in the values your mentor gives you, or that you find at:
# Firebase console > Project settings > General > Your apps > SDK setup and configuration
#
# Named `.env.production.local` (not `.env.local`) on purpose: Vite only loads
# it for `npm run build` (a "production" mode build), never for `npm run dev`
# or `npm run build:staging`. That means `npm run dev` always uses the
# emulators, even after you've set this up for a deploy.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
